(A `value` parameter passed on to a list parameter is a `value` like any
 other: the list parameter receives a copy of its list.)
To 'add to' with a list called items.
    append "c" to items.

To 'outer' with a value called v.
    'add to' of v.
    Print "v: {v}".

a value called box is ["a"].
'outer' of box.
Print "box: {box}".
